1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:05,126
HSK Pilot is a bounded WHSK to USDT trading assistant for HashKey Chain.

2
00:00:05,176 --> 00:00:07,639
You approve the trading limits once.

3
00:00:07,689 --> 00:00:12,735
An on-chain Guard contract then enforces every trade inside those limits,

4
00:00:12,785 --> 00:00:16,924
and every decision and fill leaves evidence you can inspect.

5
00:00:17,774 --> 00:00:19,385
This is the public demo.

6
00:00:19,435 --> 00:00:24,647
It runs in simulation mode, with synthetic balances and live funds disabled.

7
00:00:24,697 --> 00:00:26,862
The health endpoint confirms it:

8
00:00:26,912 --> 00:00:33,300
data mode simulation, live funds false, chain one seventy seven, and the AI model configured.

9
00:00:34,150 --> 00:00:36,218
Here is the AI decision engine.

10
00:00:36,268 --> 00:00:42,095
When I ask for a decision, the server calls the model, GPT-6 Luna through Sub2API.

11
00:00:42,145 --> 00:00:44,282
The key never leaves the server.

12
00:00:44,332 --> 00:00:48,450
The model only chooses hold or rebalance and a size fraction,

13
00:00:48,500 --> 00:00:50,979
and the panel shows the source as AI.

14
00:00:51,029 --> 00:00:56,650
If the model is unavailable or rate limited, a rule-based fallback answers instead,

15
00:00:56,700 --> 00:00:57,812
clearly labelled.

16
00:00:58,662 --> 00:01:00,664
The size is clamped by the Guard.

17
00:01:00,714 --> 00:01:04,332
The server first builds the trade the Guard's limits allow:

18
00:01:04,382 --> 00:01:08,559
the single buy limit, budgets, inventory cap, cooldown and slippage.

19
00:01:08,609 --> 00:01:11,481
The AI can only take a fraction of that amount,

20
00:01:11,531 --> 00:01:15,025
so it can never suggest more than the Guard would accept.

21
00:01:15,075 --> 00:01:17,014
The decisions are advisory only.

22
00:01:17,064 --> 00:01:19,252
There is no signer path from the AI.

23
00:01:20,102 --> 00:01:24,582
On mainnet, the Trading Session Guard is deployed on HashKey Chain,

24
00:01:24,632 --> 00:01:27,354
and its source is verified on Blockscout.

25
00:01:27,404 --> 00:01:30,599
Every execute call needs two EIP-712 signatures,

26
00:01:30,649 --> 00:01:36,820
one from a strategy signer and one from a risk signer, bound to the session, policy version,

27
00:01:36,870 --> 00:01:39,254
nonce, quote age and minimum output.

28
00:01:39,304 --> 00:01:43,716
The owner can pause the Guard and withdraw everything at any time.

29
00:01:44,566 --> 00:01:46,754
Here is the real mainnet trade.

30
00:01:46,804 --> 00:01:52,674
This execute transaction sold one WHSK for USDT through HSKSwap, inside the Guard.

31
00:01:52,724 --> 00:01:57,944
The quote was eighty seven thousand one hundred fifty two raw USDT units,

32
00:01:57,994 --> 00:02:02,636
and the fill matched it exactly, above the signed minimum output.

33
00:02:03,486 --> 00:02:07,881
The Guard's transaction list on Blockscout shows the full sequence:

34
00:02:07,931 --> 00:02:11,397
deployment, start session, execute, and withdraw all,

35
00:02:11,447 --> 00:02:14,317
with the WHSK funding under token transfers.

36
00:02:14,367 --> 00:02:19,226
Two earlier attempts stopped on false alarms in our own monitoring script,

37
00:02:19,276 --> 00:02:21,747
and the funds were returned each time.

38
00:02:21,797 --> 00:02:27,652
After the final run, the Guard was emptied and paused, with all allowances reset to zero.

39
00:02:28,502 --> 00:02:31,793
Everything is open source under the MIT license,

40
00:02:31,843 --> 00:02:36,247
with the evidence files and transaction links in the repository.

41
00:02:36,297 --> 00:02:36,943
HSK Pilot:

42
00:02:36,993 --> 00:02:40,284
your limits, every decision, checkable on chain.
